From c146dc0b8d896a6f27808606f1bb3f4bcd74cecc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 16:39:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Close the 4th small gap: node role tags replace
 name-convention guessing

A real event source no longer has to rename its stops to Sentinel's
*queue*/agent_a-g convention to be understood -- it can declare what a
stop IS directly. ivr_events gains an optional per-event 'role' field
(NODE_ROLE_QUEUE/AGENT/ESCALATION). Tagging is per-stop, not
all-or-nothing: an untagged stop still falls back to the exact name-guess
behavior this module always had. An unrecognized role or a node tagged
two different roles across repeated visits both fail loud in
_validate_ivr_events, same posture the rest of the contract already has.

IcebergJourney carries the tags through as node_roles (node -> role),
empty on the fallback heuristic path (it knows no roles). Investigated
all three originally-flagged consumers before touching them:

- production_harness.py's live first_queue detection (line 441) -- LIVE
  PATH, checked on every real call. Now checks node_roles before the
  'queue' substring guess.
- sentinel_core.py's prescribe_queue_reordering -- NOT called from the
  production harness, only exercised in its own tests. Fixed anyway for
  consistency; call_outcomes dicts may now carry an optional 'node_roles'
  key the same shape IcebergJourney produces.
- observe_perceive_core.py's PerceiveCore.infer_outcome (RESOLUTION_NODES
  literal-membership check, the most brittle of the three -- an exact
  match against 7 hardcoded names) -- also NOT called from the production
  harness currently (ObserveCore.get_emotional_state is used there, not
  PerceiveCore.infer_outcome). Fixed anyway, gains an optional node_roles
  parameter defaulting to None (unchanged behavior when absent).

8 new tests across 4 files, including one live-path test proving
process_call() correctly attributes intent to a role-tagged node whose
name would never have matched the old convention. Full suite 704
passed / 6 skipped, twice back-to-back. Ruff and bandit clean. None of
the four touched files are in the governance code-hash surface, so no
ledger reset was needed this time (unlike the previous two commits).
